// SANBASINCLEAN-001 golden: three agents share ONE wash basin at a
// self-sufficient camp for 1440 ticks under REALISTIC food/water competition
// (hunger and thirst are NOT zeroed, unlike survival-sanitation-breakdown-1440).
//
// The basin uses the default full-scale `max_effective_dirtiness: 1000`, so the
// HARD `TargetWashBasinNotTooDirty` block (at 1000) is effectively unreachable.
// Instead, the agents' default `wash_worthwhile_effectiveness_floor` (500‰)
// triggers the proactive clean_wash_basin maintenance once shared use drives the
// basin's effectiveness below half. This proves the FND-11 dampener engages in
// the realistic-competition regime where it previously stalled: agents clean the
// degraded-but-still-usable basin before it becomes useless, keeping dirtiness
// recoverable while still having to interleave eating and drinking.
//
// The camp is self-sufficient (water + apples + basin all co-located) so the run
// isolates the proactive-cleaning loop under need competition rather than travel.
// Social/tell behaviour is disabled per agent (tell_profile zeros) so the run
// stays a pure survival-contention proof.
(
    seed: 1760001,
    compaction_interval: 240,
    places: [
        (
            // Camp + Farm: a riverside farming camp. The Farm tag lets agents
            // relieve themselves outdoors (no latrine here), and wilderness
            // relief's dirtiness penalty reinforces the wash loop that degrades
            // the shared basin.
            name: "Riverside Camp",
            tags: [Camp, Farm],
            place_dirtiness: (value: 0, decay_per_tick: 2, dirtiness_per_use: 40),
            sleep_quality: (shelter: Roofed, ground_comfort: Soft, recovery_modifier: 1000),
        ),
    ],
    agents: [
